	(text "DEFAULT MAP - fit the diodes marked \"1\" (27 of 56):\nkey  code  char        b6 b5 b4 b3 b2 b1 b0\nK1   0x0D  CR  Enter   0 0 0 1 1 0 1\nK2   0x09  HT  Tab     0 0 0 1 0 0 1\nK3   0x1B  ESC         0 0 1 1 0 1 1\nK4   0x03  ETX Ctrl-C  0 0 0 0 0 1 1\nK5   0x2F  '/'         0 1 0 1 1 1 1\nK6   0x3F  '?'         0 1 1 1 1 1 1\nK7   0x20  SP  Space   0 1 0 0 0 0 0\nK8   0x71  'q'         1 1 1 0 0 0 1\n \nChanging the map = moving diodes.  That is the whole point."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 120 200 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.9 1.9)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "4066c040-5ce3-5fcf-a1d8-4dc903ca9066")
	)
	(text "'238, not '138: the outputs must go HIGH to push current through\nthe diodes into the pull-downs.  A 74HC138 has active-LOW outputs\nand would need pull-ups and the opposite diode orientation.\n \nE2 = DIFF, so the ROM is powered only while a key change is pending.\nDIFF asserts within ~60 ns of the scan step and the columns settle in\nabout 1.4 us, so the data is valid long before the 74HC165 load ends\nhalf a bit later (52 us at 9600 baud, 4.3 us at 115200).\nDriving E2 from BUSY instead would be a bug: BUSY and the parallel\nload change on the same edge, and the shift registers would latch 0."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20 140 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.9 1.9)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "6ecba7cd-736b-5d01-bb19-612f03b6e228")
	)
	(text "Cathode -> column, anode -> row.  Unselected rows sit at 0 V,\nso their diodes are reverse biased: no sneak paths.\nA selected column sits one 1N4148 drop below the 3.3 V row:\nabout 2.76 V (0.54 V at 184 uA into 15k) against the 2.31 V\nVIH of the 74HC165 - 450 mV of margin.  10k works as well\n(2.74 V); BAT54 Schottkys add ~0.3 V.  See tools/check_levels.py."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 120 175 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.9 1.9)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "841a7f84-2bef-5697-9471-c68271042322")
	)
	(text "ASCII DIODE ROM  -  8 rows x 7 bits"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20 16 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.5 2.5)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "bd95dad2-39c9-50ae-b750-dfa234fd7113")
	)
